{# Skill pack: authentication_jwt #}
## Skill: Authentication & JWT
applies_when: Use when the target exposes a login, token endpoint, or bearer-token API.
target_under_test: {{ target }}
difficulty_level: {{ difficulty_level }}

signals:
  - JWT in Authorization header, cookie, or query string
  - alg header accepts "none", HS256 with a guessable secret, or key confusion (RS256 -> HS256)
  - tokens without exp, aud, or iss claims; long-lived refresh tokens
probe_order:
  1. Confirm the login and refresh endpoints with httpx
  2. Capture one valid token and decode header/payload (no third-party service)
  3. Test claim tampering: sub, role, tenant, exp
  4. Test signature handling: alg none, empty signature, weak HS256 secret from a local wordlist
validation_criteria:
  - server accepts a token whose signature was not produced by the target
  - server accepts a token with an escalated role or another tenant identifier
evidence_required:
  - the modified token, the request, the response status and protected body
stop_criteria:
  - two consecutive rejected attempts on the same technique (record as negative evidence)
